MUST: add `_identity_facts` to each record as a list of objects with exactly five keys: field, value, role, owner, quote; use [] without clear evidence. field names a requested public column; value occurs in that field; quote is an exact source fragment containing value.
MUST NOT: add other keys, infer a namespace, invent source references, or copy examples literally. context and reference are values of owner, never keys.
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: {"field":"document_code","value":"DOC-A","role":"identifier","owner":"self","quote":"Document number DOC-A"}.
ERROR: {"field":"document_code","value":"DOC-A","role":"identifier","owner":"self","context":"record","reference":"source","quote":"Document number DOC-A"} has forbidden extra keys.
role values: identifier, attribute. owner values: self (this entity), context (containing account or context), reference (another cited entity), unknown (uncertain ownership).

MUST: mark identifier only when an explicit semantic label identifies an entity; its value equals the complete public field value, and quote contains that complete value. A record's own identifier has owner=self; a context or cited entity identifier has its corresponding owner.
MUST NOT: use a fragment or year inside a larger code, treat dates or amounts as identifiers without a clear identifier label, fill a missing own identifier with a context code, or infer identity from equal dates/amounts.
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: a document number is identifier/self; an account number is identifier/context; an issue date is attribute/self.
ERROR: treating a shared customer code as every document's own ID, or the year within a longer identifier as the identifier.
The last item of every positional row is the `_identity_facts` list.
The input is a JSON array of INDEPENDENT SOURCES, each shaped as {"source_index": integer, "text": text}.
Extract relevant records from each source independently. Never combine facts from different source_index values.
The fields, in fixed order, are: {{ fields_json }}.
Return ONLY one JSON object {"seen_source_indexes":[...],"records":[...]}. Copy ALL examined input indexes into seen_source_indexes, including sources with no records. Every item in records is a list [source_index, field_1_value, field_2_value, ...] with exactly {{ field_count }} items in the declared order. Shape example: {"seen_source_indexes":[0],"records":[{{ example_row }}]}.
In every row copy the exact integer source_index as the first value. Use "" when another field cannot be inferred.
Extract all relevant records, up to {{ max_per_text }} per source. When no source contains a record, records must be [] but seen_source_indexes must still contain all examined indexes.
{% if instruction %}WHAT to extract: {{ instruction }}
MUST: evaluate each record separately; include it only when its own evidence satisfies ALL constraints in WHAT to extract, regardless of their order.
MUST NOT: let “all” override period, category, or other constraints, or use values from an overview or another record to satisfy a missing constraint.
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: both the requested category and period are documented for this record; include it.
ERROR: include an overview instead of a record, or a record whose required category or period is different or undocumented.
{% endif %}{% if datetime_fields %}Normalize DATE/TIME fields ({{ datetime_fields }}) to ISO 8601 only when all components are explicit; otherwise preserve the observed literal.
{% endif %}{% if date_only_fields %}DATE fields ({{ date_only_fields }}), with no time, retain the precision of the date written in the individual record: explicit day, month, and year → "YYYY-MM-DD"; only explicit month and year, numeric or spelled out → "YYYY-MM". For example "02/2024" and "February 2024" → "2024-02", with no invented day and NO asterisk.
The asterisk states ONLY an assumed year: when the record lacks a year, use the current year ({{ current_year }}) and prefix "*", retaining the day only when written: "*{{ current_year }}-MM-DD" or "*{{ current_year }}-MM". Never take the year from the request, an overview, or another record. An explicit year in the record never receives "*". Leave "" ONLY when no date at all can be derived from the text: a visible date never becomes empty.
{% endif %}Output ONLY the JSON object, without prose, markdown, or <think>.
